    {
      "bbox": [
        337,
        1591,
        1813,
        2230
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The existing state law (Section 63 of the Public Officers\nLaw) accords such privileges only to veterans who \"served in the\nArmy or the Navy or Marine Corps of the United States . . . during\nWorld War I or during World War II\". This order is designed to\nremedy this omission so that veterans of our armed forces who\nserved in the Korean War need not be denied Armistice Day holiday\nprivileges until the state law is properly amended.",
